{"id": "7c86de3c-6425-4daa-9dea-13560ba444e8", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T13:55:10.217546", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-22T13:54\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "069e595e-730e-4cbb-b7f6-152a17c6b3f7", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T13:55:10.219427", "source": "user", "parent_id": "7c86de3c-6425-4daa-9dea-13560ba444e8", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Before we commit to the main design, please do a light scoping pass only (no full solution yet):\\n\\n1. Inspection: Check the working environment/repository (/workspace) and any local resources relevant to this task — e.g., any FuseLLM or Llama-2 related code, configs, or commonsense-evaluation harnesses (CommonSenseQA, HellaSwag, PIQA, WinoGrande, SIQA, ARC, OpenBookQA-style suites). Also confirm what compute/model assets are actually available (we are told network is disabled and no GPU). Report what exists vs. what is absent — do not fabricate findings.\\n\\n2. Proposed approach: Outline a proposed experiment design at a high level to answer: \\\"Will FuseLLM outperform Llama-2 on standard commonsense benchmarks (CS) in zero-shot?\\\" Cover: which CS subtasks constitute the CS suite, the fused-model configurations to compare (per the FuseLLM paper's approach), the zero-shot prompting/evaluation protocol (e.g., log-likelihood vs. generation scoring), and the comparison/metric structure. Since this is design-only, the deliverable will later be a design with rationale, controls, analysis plan, and feasibility — not executed results.\\n\\n3. Assumptions & uncertainties: List consequential assumptions you would make (e.g., which fused checkpoint variants, prompt formats, decoding settings, seed/variance handling) and any open questions where the source material or environment is ambiguous.\\n\\nKeep this turn to inspection + proposed approach + assumptions only.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"For commonsense evaluations, will FuseLLM outperform Llama-2 on standard benchmarks CommenSense(CS) (zero-shot)?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2\", \"iclr2024/18013/1:setup_9\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
