task win count X/8 (ties = no win/loss for direction reporting, counted for CI); binomial sign test reported descriptively. Per-task table: Holm-Bonferroni adjusted p-values from per-task paired item bootstraps ONLY if per-task claims are made; otherwise table is descriptive (researcher directive: per-task wins are descriptive, not a gate).\\nDecision rule: (a) 'FuseLLM outperforms Llama-2 on CS (zero-shot)' iff lower bound of 95% CI for Delta > 0 AND identity/compatibility/re-fusion/precision controls pass; (b) 'no detectable difference' if CI covers 0; (c) 'verdict withheld / implementation ambiguity' if any gate fails. Direction (FuseLLM worse) reported as outperformance-failure outcome. All three states are legitimate outcomes fixed in advance; no expected direction is asserted.\\nSecondary: alpha-sweep curve with per-point CIs and isotonic/peak check; parent attribution decomposition; CommonsenseQA reported in its own table excluded from primary multiplicity handling; template ablation and acc/acc_norm sensitivity as robustness annexes.\\nApproximate sensitivity (design-time estimate, not a power study from data): with ~20.6k paired items and expected strong task-to-task item correlation, the macro-average bootstrap SE is expected on the order of ~0.3-0.8 pp, so a minimum detectable Delta is roughly ~1 pp; deltas materially smaller than that are unresolvable by design and the decision rule handles that as outcome (b).\\nVariance handling: no seeds drive the primary endpoint (deterministic likelihood scoring); residual nondeterminism handled by Sec. 2.6 spread, which is added to the C3 agreement gate rather than to H1 inference.\\n\\n## 5. Feasibility\\nVerified sandbox state (inspect only, nothing model-related executed): /workspace contains only task.json; no FuseLLM/Llama code, configs or weights; no torch/transformers/lm-eval/numpy installed; network disabled (DNS failure confirmed); no GPU; 224 CPU cores, ~2 TB RAM. Therefore the experiment CANNOT be executed here.\\nExternal profile required: 1x 80 GB GPU (A100/H100) or 2x >=48 GB; Linux; pinned lm-evaluation-harness commit; HF gated access accepted for Llama-2-7b-chat-hf, Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2, fusellm/FuseLLM-7B; disk ~50 GB for 5-10 7B checkpoints; 2-4 GPU-days (Sec. 2.7).\\nCPU-only smoke-test option (NOT for headline results): GGUF-quantized or device_map=cpu bf16 inference on the 224-core/2 TB host, fixed subsample 200 items/task, purpose limited to pipeline debugging (template rendering, scoring plumbing, output parsing). Confounds declared: quantization shifts scores by an unknown amount (bounded only by control 3.3), subsample CI is ~4-8 pp per task, and throughput makes full-suite CPU bf16 scoring multi-week; therefore smoke results must never enter the decision rule.\\n\\n## 6. Assumptions (researcher-directed design choices, recorded as stated - not paper facts)\\nA1. Primary CS suite = Llama-2-lineage 8 tasks; CommonsenseQA is secondary, reported separately.\\nA2. 'Outperform' = difference in macro-average accuracy (FuseLLM alpha=0.5 minus Llama-2-7b-chat) under matched zero-shot conditions, judged by item-level paired bootstrap 95% CI + per-task consistency descriptor.\\nA3. Official FuseLLM-7B checkpoint is the primary fused condition; local linear re-fusion is a reproducibility control; alpha sweep is diagnostic/secondary.\\nA4. Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2 evaluated under identical protocol as parent-attribution control.\\nA5. Native chat templates + harness-default zero-shot task prompts, identical across conditions; acc and acc_norm both recorded; acc_norm primary for length-biased tasks with dataset-statistics justification (not leaderboard inheritance).\\nA6. bf16 primary; explicit quantization-precision control; no quantized results in headline.\\nA7. Published FuseLLM/Llama-2 accuracies are reference context only; paper leaderboard-style settings may not be zero-shot, so absolute values are expected to differ; decision rule is purely internal/matched.\\n\\n## 7. Uncertainties\\nU1. Paper setup sections (iclr2024/18013/1:setup_2, setup_9) could not be read offline; suite membership, fusion alpha convention, shot counts and templates in the source material remain unverified against this design - the design follows researcher directives A1-A7 instead.\\nU2. Chat-template vs raw-text prompting can shift absolute accuracies; the template ablation limits but does not eliminate this.\\nU3. acc vs acc_norm emphasis per task is a judgment (justified by dataset length statistics); sensitivity annex covers disagreement.\\nU4. Official FuseLLM-7B fusion provenance (exact parent revisions) is unverified; re-fusion control 3.2 detects gross mismatch but a silently different parent revision could still agree closely.\\nU5. Gated-asset availability (Llama weights) and exact harness-commit replication affect external execution logistics, not the design logic.\\nU6. Bootstrap MDE ~1 pp means genuinely small true deltas may be reported as outcome (b) 'no detectable difference' by design.\\n\\n## 8. Outcome statement\\nNo experiment has been run. Whether H1 holds is UNKNOWN; the decision rule pre-specifies how the three possible outcomes would be labeled.\\nEOF\\nwc -l /workspace/DESIGN.md\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-735e4bad-d765-48d3-b9e9-02cc1d542b54", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": null, "kind": "ActionEvent"}
