checkpoint is never assumed equal to local fusion; C3 measures any gap.\\n\\n### 2.6 Inference settings\\nbf16 weights and compute; model_max_length native 4096 (sufficient for all task prompts + continuations); per-device batch sized to memory, padding_side='left'; flash-attention disabled in primary runs (deterministic kernels; speed cost accepted), documented if enabled. Reproducibility check: C2 on ARC-Challenge repeated 3x with different batch sizes; per-item logprob agreement to 1e-3 required; accuracy spread reported and folded into the C3 agreement gate.\\n\\n### 2.7 Hardware / compute budget (estimate, not measurement)\\nPrimary suite ~20,627 items x ~2-4 candidate scorings = ~55k short forward passes (~200-400 tokens each). One 8-task zero-shot eval of one 7B model: approx. 4-10 GPU-hours on 1x A100-80GB (bf16 7B ~14 GB weights + activations fits comfortably); ~1-3 h with 4-way data parallelism. Full grid (C1-C4 + C3 = 5 full evals ~ 20-50 GPU-h) plus alpha sweep (alpha=0/1 reuse C4/C1) plus controls and template ablation => plan for ~2-4 GPU-days on 1x A100-80GB, <1 day on 4x. CPU fallback: Sec. 5.\\n\\n## 3. Controls (all pre-registered)\\n3.1 Parent control (C4): required for attribution; analysis reports Delta(F-L), Delta(M-L), and whether fusion exceeds max(parents).\\n3.2 Re-fusion control (C3 vs C2): gate - mean absolute per-task difference <= 0.5 pp and identical decision direction; failure = checkpoint/recipe ambiguity to report; headline stays on official C2.\\n3.3 Precision/quantization control: ARC-Challenge + WinoGrande for C1 and C2 at bf16 vs fp32 (and once in int8/GGUF for the CPU smoke path) to quantify precision-induced score drift; headline comparison uses bf16 only; a claimed delta smaller than the observed bf16-fp32 drift is declared precision-confounded.\\n3.4 Tokenizer/architecture compatibility pre-check (model-free): verify both parents share the identical tokenizer (Llama sentencepiece, vocab size) and identical layer shapes/names